                            <comment id="471671" author="adilger" created="Tue, 16 Sep 2025 18:03:14 +0000">&lt;p&gt;This looks like &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19323" title="lnet_selftest.sh support for ipv6 " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19323"&gt;LU-19323&lt;/a&gt; because lnet-selftest does not support IPv6 yet.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="471682" author="pjones" created="Tue, 16 Sep 2025 19:02:57 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Should we just be skipping the test for now then?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="472710" author="adilger" created="Wed, 24 Sep 2025 04:22:52 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Yes, test will be skipped by patch &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/61337" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/61337&lt;/a&gt; ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19323" title="lnet_selftest.sh support for ipv6 " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19323"&gt;LU-19323&lt;/a&gt; tests: add more sanity-lnet subtests into IPv6 except list").&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="474495" author="yujian" created="Thu, 9 Oct 2025 23:49:00 +0000">&lt;p&gt;After &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19323" title="lnet_selftest.sh support for ipv6 " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19323"&gt;LU-19323&lt;/a&gt; is resolved, the subtest can be removed from the always except list.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="498328" author="adilger" created="Wed, 22 Jul 2026 10:16:30 +0000">&lt;p&gt;tickets for tests that are still being being skipped by &lt;tt&gt;always_except&lt;/tt&gt; should not be closed&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
